{
  "id": "strategic_game.mixed_strategy",
  "title": "Mixed Strategy",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "strategic_game/strategic_game_mixed_strategy.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Mixed Strategy</h1>\n<p>For a finite or measurable strategy set $S_i$, a mixed strategy of player $i$ is a\nprobability measure on $S_i$. In the finite case the mixed strategy space is the\nsimplex\n$$\n  \\Delta(S_i).\n$$\nPure strategies are identified with Dirac measures. A mixed profile is an element\n$$\n  \\sigma=(\\sigma_i)_{i\\in I}\\in \\prod_{i\\in I}\\Delta(S_i).\n$$</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
